{
  "id": "size-constancy",
  "term": "size constancy",
  "definition": "Size constancy is the perceptual process of judging an object’s size by combining viewing distance, the size of its retinal image, and surrounding visual context, so perceived size can remain relatively stable despite changes in how large the image appears on the eye.",
